{"total_count":6,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472/events","html_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472","id":1819217287,"node_id":"I_kwDOAacf885sbw2H","number":6472,"title":"NOTICE: Upcoming API changes to experimental Name Resolver (`resolver`) and LB Policy (`balancer`) packages","user":{"login":"dfawley","id":26072277,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDcyMjc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26072277?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley","html_url":"https://github.com/dfawley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfawley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":299649128,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyOTk2NDkxMjg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/labels/Type:%20API%20Change","name":"Type: API Change","color":"bfdadc","default":false,"description":"Breaking API changes (experimental APIs only!)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":528927681,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1Mjg5Mjc2ODE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/labels/P2","name":"P2","color":"610B0B","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7326498984,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAacf888AAAABtLGAqA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/labels/Area:%20Resolvers/Balancers","name":"Area: Resolvers/Balancers","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Includes LB policy & NR APIs, resolver/balancer/picker wrappers, LB policy impls and utilities.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2023-07-24T22:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T06:07:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"To support the upcoming IPv4/IPv6 Dualstack design ([gRFC A61](https://github.com/grpc/proposal/pull/356)), some changes will be required in the `resolver` and `balancer`.  We will also be taking this opportunity to streamline the APIs a bit, in particular improving the LB policy API to make it easier to build and manage child LB policies (used extensively for our xDS support).\n\nThe design is not finalized, however, the following changes are currently planned:\n\n* Dualstack support:\n  * [x] ~~Add an abstraction for \"endpoints\" in resolver results, which will each contain a list of addresses (#6471)~~\n  * [x] ~~The default `pick_first` LB policy will perform the \"happy eyeballs\" algorithm ([RFC8305](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8305)) to establish a connection (https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7725, https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7742)~~\n  * [x] ~~Update every leaf LB policy to use `pick_first` as its child to handle endpoint connections~~\n    * [x] ~leastrequest (https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7969)~\n    * [x] ~weighted_round_robin (https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7826)~\n    * [x] ~~roundrobin~~\n    * [x] ~~ringhash~~\n  * [x] ~~Internally change the implementation of health checking so it applies in `pick_first` instead of inside the `SubConn` (https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7780, https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7832, https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/pull/7900)~~\n    * [ ] Make the base balancer to use the health listener instead. Presently, [it relies](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/blob/1ed87ec0fb2a61656d13965a8b3aeb49c98c6e4b/balancer/base/base.go#L58-L62) on the health checks done inside the subchannel.\n    * [ ] Remove health checking implementation in the channel.\n  * [ ] Avoid requesting re-resolution on subchannel failure, making it the responsibility of the LB policy (#7534).\n\n* General improvements / cleanups\n  * [x] ~~Provide `SubConn` state updates via a callback instead of by calling `balancer.UpdateSubConnState` (#6481)~~\n  * [x] ~~Deprecate `ClientConn.RemoveSubConn` and add `balancer.SubConn.Shutdown` as its replacement (#6493)~~\n    * [ ] Remove `ClientConn.RemoveSubConn`\n  * [x] ~~Deprecate `resolver.Address.BalancerAttributes` and add `resolver.Endpoint.Attributes` as its replacement (#6471)~~\n    * [ ]  Remove `resolver.Address.BalancerAttributes`. Presently used for authority override and backed service metric labels.\n  * [ ] Remove `resolver.Address.Metadata`.\n    * The `State.Attributes` or `Endpoint.Attributes` fields should be used to communicate between resolver and LB policy.  The `Address.Attributes` field should be used to communicate with the transport layer.\n  * [ ] Remove the ability to specify multiple addresses per `SubConn`\n    * This requires changing grpclb to delegate to the pick first LB policy instead of relying on the subchannel's implementation of pick first.\n  * [ ] Remove `SubConn.UpdateAddresses` and `ClientConn.UpdateAddresses`\n  * [ ] Introduce requirement that LB policies that create `SubConn`s be responsible for shutting them down when `Balancer.Close` is called.\n    * Note that with `pick_first` as the universal leaf policy, only `pick_first` will need to be updated to do this.\n    * This can simplify graceful switch, or other parent policies that might be tracking created subchannels for this purpose.\n\nWe will do our best to make these changes in a way that allows several releases / months between adding the new version of an API and removing the old version.\n\n**Please keep in mind that all these APIs are still experimental, even the newly added ones.  Until we can guarantee long-term support for them, they will remain this way.  Note that any _packages_ outside this repo that use an experimental symbol or import an experimental package should be considered experimental themselves, as the removal of a symbol would break compilation of that entire package.**","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/6472/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/4881","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/4881/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/4881/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grpc/grpc-go/issues/4881/events","html_url":"https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/issues/4881","id":1027671161,"node_id":"I_kwDOAacf8849QQR5","number":4881,"title":"balancer: SubConn doesn't recover if UpdateAddress() is called with an empty list","user":{"login":"menghanl","id":960845,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MDg0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/960845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/menghanl","html_url":